# ABP Background Jobs

## Creating a Background Job
```csharp
// 1. Define job arguments
public class EmailSendingArgs
{
    public string EmailAddress { get; set; }
    public string Subject { get; set; }
    public string Body { get; set; }
}

// 2. Create the job
public class EmailSendingJob : AsyncBackgroundJob<EmailSendingArgs>, ITransientDependency
{
    private readonly IEmailSender _emailSender;

    public EmailSendingJob(IEmailSender emailSender)
    {
        _emailSender = emailSender;
    }

    public override async Task ExecuteAsync(EmailSendingArgs args)
    {
        await _emailSender.SendAsync(args.EmailAddress, args.Subject, args.Body);
    }
}
```

## Enqueuing Jobs
```csharp
await _backgroundJobManager.EnqueueAsync(
    new EmailSendingArgs
    {
        EmailAddress = "user@example.com",
        Subject = "Hello",
        Body = "..."
    },
    delay: TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5) // Optional delay
);
```

## Job Name Attribute
```csharp
[BackgroundJobName("emails")]
public class EmailSendingArgs { }
```

## Exception Handling
- Don't hide exceptions - they trigger automatic retry
- Use `ICancellationTokenProvider` for cancellable jobs

## Disable Job Execution
```csharp
Configure<AbpBackgroundJobOptions>(options =>
{
    options.IsJobExecutionEnabled = false;
});
```

## Integrations
- Hangfire: `Volo.Abp.BackgroundJobs.Hangfire`
- RabbitMQ: `Volo.Abp.BackgroundJobs.RabbitMQ`
- Quartz: `Volo.Abp.BackgroundJobs.Quartz`
